   "text": "The search has stopped, with the best specification being **[24+, 0-]** at in-sample Sharpe **1.0637**. This is a 2-feature spec: long feature 24, short feature 0, equal-weighted.\n\nNow let me think about the out-of-sample Sharpe prediction. In-sample Sharpe of ~1.06 for a 2-feature combination found via a short, disciplined search (only 3 moves, one of which was rejected) is reasonably modest \u2014 not the result of exhaustive overfitting across all 40 features in combination. Still, in-sample Sharpes are optimistic relative to true OOS performance due to:\n\n1. Selection effects (picked best of 80 single features, then best-improving pair)\n2. Only 2 features used \u2014 less overfitting risk than a full 3-feature dredge\n3. Costs are already netted into the measure, so the degradation from costs is already priced in\n\nA common rule of thumb is that OOS Sharpe degrades to roughly 50-70% of in-sample Sharpe for modestly-searched specifications like this. I'll center my estimate around 0.55-0.65 of 1.0637, with meaningful uncertainty."
